WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.693
Category entry points are the cues that send people into a category:

00:00:03.743 --> 00:00:04.566
occasions,

00:00:04.616 --> 00:00:05.416
needs,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.676
places and people.

00:00:06.726 --> 00:00:07.526
The more of them a brand links to,

00:00:07.175 --> 00:00:10.762
the more often it comes to mind.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.198
Three people want a snack.

00:00:13.248 --> 00:00:14.601
One is studying late,

00:00:14.651 --> 00:00:15.451
one is on a road trip,

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:17.242
one just needs a break.

00:00:17.292 --> 00:00:19.425
KitKat owns the break.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:20.933
To grow,

00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:23.255
KitKat can link itself to new entry points,

00:00:23.305 --> 00:00:25.166
like after study or a road trip.

00:00:25.216 --> 00:00:28.427
Each new link is another moment it comes to mind.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:30.321
Use it like this:

00:00:30.371 --> 00:00:31.972
list the category's entry points,

00:00:32.022 --> 00:00:33.599
see which ones rivals own,

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.147
and claim an under-used one.
